IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cm64-nouns`
IMPORT `cm64-cross-references`

-- Row il-64. The controls hold, and the recorded facts about the two defects are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their six failing assertions are in cm64-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in cm64-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound controls`

-- I1 control: the three subsections that the same sentence of s 21ב(ג) cites after the semicolon are there, and the citation points at what it says.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite subsections (ב1), (ב2) and (ב3)`)
#ASSERT `the target has everything the citing words name` (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite subsections (ב1), (ב2) and (ב3)`)
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite subsections (ב1), (ב2) and (ב3)`)'s `how many things the citing words name` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite subsections (ב1), (ב2) and (ב3)`)'s `how many of them the target has` EQUALS 3
-- I2 control: the defined term of s 6ח4(ב) is defined in s 6ח4(ג).
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the term בעל זיכיון, to its definition in s 6ח4(ג)`)
#ASSERT `the target has everything the citing words name` (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the term בעל זיכיון, to its definition in s 6ח4(ג)`)

§ `Tests of what the records say (I1)`

-- The section number cited is 6ל, and the instrument gave the section the number 21ג.
#ASSERT (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)'s `the number the section bore before` EQUALS "6ל"
#ASSERT (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)'s `the number the instrument gave the section` EQUALS "21ג"
#ASSERT (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)'s `the number the citing words cite` EQUALS "6ל"
#ASSERT NOT `the number the words cite is the number the section now bears` (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)
-- The reference names one section, and the target has none of it.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)'s `how many things the citing words name` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)'s `how many of them the target has` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the text of a section that says who represents the owners of the apartments in dealings with the licensee`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a note that the section was re-marked with another number`
#ASSERT NOT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)
#ASSERT NOT `the target has everything the citing words name` (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)
-- Where each reading came from: the re-marking from the official page, the crop deposited; the cited number from the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)'s `the re-marking was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)'s `the number the citing words cite was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official page for the re-marking, the consolidation only for the text of the section it now stands in`

§ `Tests of what the records say (I2)`

-- The section cited is 6יב2, and the repealing section lists 6יב1 to 6יב4, so the section cited is among the sections repealed.
#ASSERT (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)'s `the stem of the sections repealed` EQUALS "6יב"
#ASSERT (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)'s `the first number after the stem that is repealed` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)'s `the last number after the stem that is repealed` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)'s `the number after the stem of the section the citing words cite` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the section cited is among the sections repealed` (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)
#ASSERT NOT `the section cited stands outside the repealed numbers` (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)
-- The reference names one paragraph, and the target has none of it.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)'s `how many things the citing words name` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)'s `how many of them the target has` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a section repealed by another instrument`
#ASSERT NOT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)
#ASSERT NOT `the target has everything the citing words name` (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)
-- Both limbs were read from the official pages, the crops deposited.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
-- The carve-out's own period: 8 years, from the commencement of Amendment 25, whose commencement day was not read.
#ASSERT (`period: the carve-out of s 6ח4(ב)`)'s `how many years it runs for` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT (`period: the carve-out of s 6ח4(ב)`)'s `what it runs from` EQUALS "the commencement of Amendment 25"
#ASSERT NOT (`period: the carve-out of s 6ח4(ב)`)'s `the day it runs from was read`
